SCOPED LICENSING
================

This repository is licensed component-by-component, not as a whole.

Components located in a directory that contains its own LICENSE file are
licensed under the terms stated in that file. As of this writing those are:

    agent/          Apache License 2.0   supplier agent (distributed to suppliers)
    clients/sdk/python/     Apache License 2.0   buyer client library
    clients/cli/     Apache License 2.0   buyer command-line client
    clients/proto/   Apache License 2.0   wire schemas and runtime matrix

All other source code and materials in this repository -- including but not
limited to the control plane, scheduler, verification, settlement, pricing and
operational tooling -- are proprietary and may not be copied, modified,
distributed, sublicensed, or used without prior written permission.

WHY IT IS SPLIT
===============

The agent, the SDKs and the wire schemas have to be distributable: a supplier
must be able to run the agent on their own hardware and a buyer must be able to
install and inspect the client. Apache-2.0 is used for those rather than MIT
because it carries an explicit patent grant and defined attribution terms.

The marketplace itself is the product. Placing a permissive licence at the
repository root would grant permission to copy the control plane, which is the
part that is not intended to be copied.

Neither Apache-2.0 nor MIT prevents a third party from operating or reselling
the components they cover. That is understood and accepted for the client-side
components; it is the reason the server-side components are not covered.

